DFlash2 mamba-align offload/prefix-cache hit fix on vLLM 0.29.0.

Port of upstream vLLM commit fa5017a5 ("[Spec Decode] Scope prefix-cache
last-block drop to eagle-family drafters (DFlash2 offload fix)"), which landed
on vLLM main 2026-09-10 -- ONE DAY AFTER the v0.29.0 cut (09-09). It is NOT in
vllm/vllm-openai:v0.29.0 (verified: use_eagle_preserves_target_kv_cache() has
0 occurrences in the v0.29.0 tag's speculative.py) and not yet in any released
tag (v0.29.1rc0 is still 27 commits behind it).

Why (vllm#53505, CLOSED completed 2026-08-30):
  In v0.29.0, Scheduler._mamba_block_aligned_split() backs the last cache
  position off by one mamba block whenever self.use_eagle is true. use_eagle()
  returns True for dflash/dspark too, so DFlash2 receives the EAGLE
  volatile-trailing-block drop: the mamba recurrent state never materializes at
  the final block boundary, and EVERY prefix-cache and offload-tier lookup
  converges to 0 ("stores but never serves a hit"). The fix gates that back-off
  on eagle-family drafters only (eagle/eagle3/mtp). DFlash/DSpark draft from
  their OWN KV cache and never write target blocks, so they must not back off.

This is the vLLM half the FIELD_NOTES row "0.28.0 + #54165" did via a local
port of PR #54165 (still OPEN). fa5017a5 is the same intent shipped to main.
#48375 (mounted separately) is NOT sufficient -- it is single_type_kv_cache_
manager only, a different code path.

Adapted for v0.29.0 (older than fa5017a5's parent, which already had
use_eagle_block_drop()): the drop is still INLINE in _mamba_block_aligned_split
gated on self.use_eagle, so this patch (a) adds
use_eagle_preserves_target_kv_cache() to SpecDecodingConfig and (b) scopes the
inline back-off to it. Same files, same effect.

Verified: clean patch -p1 dry-run + real apply + py_compile both files +
reverse dry-run, AND sequential apply after vllm-dflash2-backport.patch.
Drop when a released vLLM tag contains fa5017a5 (watch v0.29.1/0.30.0).

----
--- a/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
+++ b/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
@@ -255,6 +255,12 @@
         )
         speculative_config = vllm_config.speculative_config
         self.use_eagle = False
+        # Only eagle-family drafters share (and look ahead into) the
+        # target's full-attention KV cache groups. DFlash/DSpark draft
+        # from their own KV cache and never write target blocks
+        # (vllm#53505). Scopes the mamba-align last-block back-off.
+        # Port of upstream fa5017a5 (not yet in v0.29.0).
+        self.use_eagle_preserves_target_kv_cache = False
         self.num_spec_tokens = vllm_config.num_speculative_tokens
         self.num_lookahead_tokens = vllm_config.num_lookahead_tokens
         # Positions past the computed tokens that the drafter reads mid-prefill.
@@ -273,6 +279,9 @@
                     vllm_num_speculative_tokens=self.num_spec_tokens,
                 )
             self.use_eagle = speculative_config.use_eagle()
+            self.use_eagle_preserves_target_kv_cache = (
+                speculative_config.use_eagle_preserves_target_kv_cache()
+            )
             if self.use_eagle:
                 self.num_prefill_lookahead = (
                     self.num_spec_tokens
@@ -414,7 +423,10 @@
         # Eagle, FullAttn prunes the last matching block, so back off one
         # block to avoid a Mamba cache miss.
         last_cache_position = request.num_tokens - request.num_tokens % block_size
-        if self.use_eagle:
+        # Only eagle-family drafters prune the last matching block; DFlash/DSpark
+        # never write target blocks (vllm#53505), so backing off orphans the final
+        # block-aligned mamba snapshot and collapses prefix-cache/offload hits to 0.
+        if self.use_eagle_preserves_target_kv_cache:
             last_cache_position = max(last_cache_position - block_size, 0)
 
         end = start + num_new_tokens
--- a/config/speculative.py
+++ b/config/speculative.py
@@ -1846,6 +1846,13 @@
         # TODO(ben): Refactor this so the naming is clearer
         return self.method in ("eagle", "eagle3", "mtp", "dflash", "dspark")
 
+    def use_eagle_preserves_target_kv_cache(self) -> bool:
+        # Only eagle-family drafters share (and look ahead into) the target's
+        # full-attention KV cache groups; DFlash/DSpark draft from their own KV
+        # cache and never write target blocks (vllm#53505). Port of upstream
+        # fa5017a5 (not yet in v0.29.0).
+        return self.method in ("eagle", "eagle3", "mtp")
+
     def use_dflash(self) -> bool:
         return self.method == "dflash"
 
